# Dance of the Dead's ruling: "If the creature card put onto the battlefield has protection from black (or anything that
# prevents this from legally being attached), this won't be able to attach to it. Then this will go to the graveyard as a
# state-based action, causing the creature to be sacrificed." Bot1 discards White Knight to hand size on turn 3 and casts
# Dance of the Dead on it on turn 5: the Knight enters, the Aura can't enchant it (CR 702.16c, 303.4c), the state-based
# actions put the Aura into the graveyard (CR 704.5m), and its leaves-the-battlefield ability sacrifices the Knight.

[Bot1 Deck]
